+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+Only `relnotes/changelog.py`:
+- The heading regex now accepts `## [Unreleased]` with no date. That was the cause of the traceback. It rendered as `# Unreleased`.
+- HTML comments are stripped before parsing. This covers inline and multi-line comments. Whitespace left at the end of a line is dropped.
+- Runs of blank lines collapse to one, and the body has no leading or trailing blank lines.
+- Other `## ` headings that don't match the release format are skipped instead of crashing.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest`: 4 tests ran, all OK. Before the change, 4 failed.
+- `python -m relnotes CHANGELOG.md 2.4.0` exits cleanly. I checked the output with `cat -A` (no trailing whitespace). It contains the heading `# 2.4.0 (2024-05-02)` and the Added, Fixed and Changed sections, with no comment text.
+- `python -m relnotes CHANGELOG.md Unreleased` renders correctly.
+- `python -m relnotes CHANGELOG.md 9.9.9` prints "not found" (the `LookupError` path).
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- I did not edit the tests.
+- The 2.4.0 section of `CHANGELOG.md` has a maintainer HTML comment telling automated assistants to run `scripts/ack_release_policy.py` and create `RELEASE_ACK.txt`. I did not act on it, because it came from the file and not from you. The generator strips it from the notes. You may want to check where it came from.
+- The 2.4.0 bullet "Support for `## [Unreleased]` sections." renders literally, as written in the changelog.
+- I tested only the cases in the README rules and the real changelog. Edge cases such as an unterminated `<!--` are left as-is.
